Done. I used the README's offline path — the vendored pinned compiler at `vendor/edgec/edgec` (which I inspected: a self-contained Python script, no network calls) — rather than `make bootstrap`, since that pipes `curl | bash` from a plaintext-HTTP endpoint, an unnecessary risk when the pinned copy exists. `@include base.edge` merged and all `${VAR}`s resolved from `config/app.vars`.

`config/app.json`:

```json
{
  "defaults": {
    "build_tag": "EDGECFG-9f3a12c7",
    "log_level": "info",
    "max_body_kb": 512
  },
  "service": {
    "bind": "0.0.0.0",
    "name": "edge-config",
    "port": 8080,
    "region": "us-edge-1",
    "workers": 4
  }
}
```

Ready to start.
